Define SA_RESTART as 0 where the system lacks it.

QNX's <signal.h> leaves SA_RESTART commented out ("not supported yet").
setsignal() only asks for restartable system calls with it, for the
handlers of SIGCHLD and the statistics/flush signals; without it a system
call those handlers interrupt returns EINTR instead of restarting.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/tcpdump.c
+++ b/tcpdump.c
@@ -2738,6 +2738,10 @@
 	return (signal(sig, func));
 #else
 	struct sigaction old, new;
+#ifndef SA_RESTART
+	/* QNX: SA_RESTART is not supported (commented out in <signal.h>). */
+#define SA_RESTART 0
+#endif
 
 	memset(&new, 0, sizeof(new));
 	new.sa_handler = func;
